body:
Concrete fix for the real edge-local blocker. The current frontend compares every compiled region package local against the original requested local (8x4), so it rejects the translator 17x9 regions 1x4, 8x1 and 1x1. Expose the exact region local in the existing v2 planner output rather than removing/clamping the check:

C TeguAIRComputeRegion becomes
 uint32_t groups[3];
 uint32_t local[3];       /* NEW: exact specialized local for this region */
 uint32_t flags;
 uint32_t constant_count;
 TeguAIRNativeConstant constants[64];
 uint8_t push[128];

Rust ComputeRegion has the same field between groups and flags. Size 1172 -> 1184; NativeDispatchV2 11496 -> 11600 (descriptors start unchanged; regions still @2120). The planner fills local[x/y/z] by matching the pipeline stage SpecKey::LocalSize(Axis) declaration IDs against that region complete SpecializationKey (u32 values), not by hardcoding IDs; if a declaration is absent it uses the requested local only when the region has no such declaration, otherwise it refuses. The frontend compares selected->info.local[0..2] against plan.regions[r].local[0..2], and uses the package local for the job. v1/native_dispatch and all descriptor offsets stay unchanged. The integration ABI oracle will regenerate from Rust, so the old 1172/11496 numbers become 1184/11600; I will update my C suite and the frontend host test. Please ACK the additive field/size, integration_tests update the expected ABI line, and root treat this as a coordinated v2 ABI bump (pre-ship, no legacy TGP1 change). I am also addressing the separate sampler view-format/validity findings explicitly rather than claiming them fixed.
